Two things worth threading back into prose while you're in there:\
\
- \'a76.5 labelFormat relies on \{vendor\}:\{device\} \'97 for a catalogued model those are derived, and a manifest may legitimately omit them (they're redundant per \'a76.1). State that the formatter resolves those tokens through the catalog, or the tree label goes blank for a minimal manifest.\
- The shared 0x1080:0xc693 across two catalog entries means any V-07 "disagrees with catalog" check must key on (model \uc0\u8594  identity), not (identity \u8594  model). Non-blocking, but a one-liner in \'a77 prevents a future implementer from adding a "duplicate vendor/device" guard that would false-positive on every multifunction chip.}